# 243 · The new dashboard's base: fxbot's UI system as a web app in control, with its shell, sign-in and checks

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.3.0](../roadmap.md#v030) · **Depends on:** [242](_completed/242-v030-review.goal)

## What

Built, and then put in question by the owner on 2026-11-10 (Decisions): its three screens came before any mockup the owner had seen, and they hold today's structure in a new look. Its plumbing stands: the app's build, the session on the API, the client, the checks. Its screens wait for mockups the owner approves. It builds design A of the [UI refresh guide](../ui-refresh-guide.md#3-how-thermite-uses-it-two-designs), which the owner chose on 2026-11-10.

The base that every screen of the new dashboard stands on ([how the web app is built](../ui-refresh-guide.md#8-how-the-web-app-is-built)):

1. **The app:** `web/` at the repository's root, a project of its own beside `docs/_site/`, with fxbot's stack: React, shadcn/ui in its `radix-nova` style, Tailwind CSS, Geist and Geist Mono, Lucide, built by Vite. Its theme is fxbot's, with four colours for states.
2. **What it may import:** `src/core`'s contracts alone. `npm run check:imports` holds it, and holds that nothing in `src/` imports the app.
3. **The client:** one typed call of a route of `src/core/api/control/`, and one reader of control's stream of changes.
4. **Sign-in:** as today, with the session good for `/v1` too, and a change sent with the session's token in a header.
5. **The shell:** the left navigation of the [guide's section 6](../ui-refresh-guide.md#6-the-new-navigation) with Needs you as a list, a screen's header, the frame of Settings, the three widths, the sheet on a phone. Every ID can be copied (goal [094](094-copy-id.goal)).
6. **Thermite's own parts,** each used by more than one screen: the state badge, the list's toolbar, a tile of figures, the empty and error states, the dialog for adding a thing.
7. **The first three screens, as the first mockups:** Home, a run's Overview and Settings, on the demo's data, in two variants of the navigation: Library, Usage and Logs as rows with words, which is mocked first, and as icons at the foot, as fxbot has them.
8. **Delivery:** control serves the built files at `/next`; control's image gains a build stage; the Content Security Policy for the app has no inline style (goal [177](177-dashboard-styles-in-its-stylesheet.goal)'s end, for the new pages).
9. **Checks:** the app's type check and linter in `npm run check`; the browser check opens the app's screens at 1,440, 820 and 390 pixels, light and dark.
10. **Mockups are screens:** a route that only a development build has shows a screen on the demo's data, with switches for its states.

## Why

The owner, 2026-11-10: "I want to utilize the UI/UX system I started for fxbot". fxbot's system is its components and how they behave; they need their framework. The faults that reached v0.1.4 came from how today's pages are built: scripts kept as strings that no linter or type check reads, and a page whose request nothing held to control's schema ([the guide](../ui-refresh-guide.md#how-the-dashboard-is-built-today)).

## Constraints

- **The old dashboard is not changed,** and stays where it is.
- **No rule of the product in the app,** and no words for states, verdicts or events: they come from control ([what the app may hold](../ui-refresh-guide.md#what-the-app-may-hold)).
- **Stock components,** made by shadcn's tool and not edited. No router, data, state or form library until its second real use.
- **Every new package is pinned and credited** in CREDITS.md, in the commit that adds it.

## Done when

- [x] The owner chose the design. Done, 2026-11-10: a web app on fxbot's own stack.
- [x] The owner chose the navigation from the two variants. Done, 2026-11-10: Library, Usage and Logs as icons at the foot.
- [x] The app builds, and control serves it at `/next`, from source in development and from control's image. Done. From source: `npm run web:build`, then any control from the source; the browser check builds it and opens it there. From control's image: the compose smoke test builds the image and reads `/next`, its script and its licences from it, and CI's job **compose-smoke** passed at 4e520ed4 (2026-11-10).
- [ ] The owner signs in and sees Home, a run's Overview and Settings on a real control, current without a reload. The app is served on a real control since 2026-11-10; the screens themselves are in question (Decisions), so this item waits for approved mockups.
- [x] The import check fails on an import the app may not make, shown by a test of the check. Done: `tests/scripts/imports.test.ts`, "the dashboard's app imports only contracts that run in a browser".
- [x] The browser check passes on the app's screens at three widths, light and dark; CI runs it. Done: `npm run acceptance:browser`, whose third part is the app (`scripts/acceptance/lib/browser-app.mjs`); CI's job **dashboard in a browser** installs the app's packages and runs it, and passed at 4e520ed4 (2026-11-10).
- [x] The app's policy has no `'unsafe-inline'`, shown by a test of the header. Done: `tests/control/api/web.test.ts`, "the page carries a fresh nonce, and a policy with no inline script or style"; the browser check fails on a style or script the policy refuses.
- [x] The goal says what the browser loads: the size of the app's script and styles. Done: [What the browser loads](#what-the-browser-loads), below.
- [x] Pages: the contributor's pages on the dashboard (how to run it, how to add a screen), CONVENTIONS.md's rule for the dashboard, and AGENTS.md's checks. Done, with the REST reference's section on the session and the app's reads, Tokens and roles, and the contributor guide (`docs/local-development.md`).

## Decisions

- 2026-11-10, the owner: accepted into v0.3.0, with the plan of goal [242](_completed/242-v030-review.goal). The dashboard is a web app on fxbot's own stack, and each recommendation of the two guides is taken; where a question is about a look, the recommendation is what is mocked first, and the owner chooses from the mockups.
- 2026-11-10, the owner, from the two variants on the demo's data: **Library, Usage and Logs are icons at the navigation's foot,** beside Settings, as fxbot has them. Each icon has its name for a pointer that rests on it and for a screen reader. The other variant, rows with words, is removed with the switch between them.
- 2026-11-10, the owner, on the built screens: "why did you not do mokcups in a claude artifact canvas first? why did you jump straight to implementation? Why didn't you try to rethink how the ui is architected, and just applied a theme to it. You never even asked yourself if things were needed or if things should be the way they are... How are you helping me simplify and make the app easier to use?" What this changes:
  - **A mockup is a picture the owner has looked at, on a design canvas, before any screen is written.** This goal's line "Mockups are screens" is withdrawn: a screen built in code is not a mockup.
  - **The three screens of this goal are not approved,** and are replaced once mockups are. Home holds the blocks of today's Overview in new components, and a run's Overview is today's without its cost cards.
  - **The structure is thought out again before any more screens:** what the owner does in a day, and for each place, tab, block and word of today's dashboard, whether it is needed. The [UI refresh guide](../ui-refresh-guide.md)'s navigation and tabs are a tidier copy of today's and are in question with it.
  - **No screen work, in this goal or in goals 245 to 252, before the owner's yes on mockups.**
- 2026-11-10: **One session, for the pages, the app and the API.** The sign-in's cookie is for every path. A session is good for each route the owner's token is good for. A change made with a session carries the session's token in the header `X-Thermite-Session-Token`; a request with an `Authorization` header is judged by its token alone, so a wrong token is refused with or without a session. The sign-in, the sign-out and "am I signed in" are routes of `/v1` (`/v1/session`).
- 2026-11-10: **The policy has a nonce, and no `'unsafe-inline'`.** This answers the plan's first question. One stock part needs a style it adds while it runs: the dialog and the sheet lock the page's scroll with a style element. Control puts a fresh nonce in the page and in its policy at each answer (`style-src 'self' 'nonce-…'`), and the app gives it to that part. No style attribute is in the app's markup; React sets a style through the browser's own style object, which the policy does not stop. The browser check fails on any style the policy refuses.
- 2026-11-10: **The browser check builds the app each time,** which answers the plan's second question: a build left over from other source can't pass, and the check opens what control serves, with control's policy. The build takes under a second.
- 2026-11-10: **Three things of goal [244](244-one-door.goal) came first, in the smallest form the three screens need.** Their contracts are in `src/core/api/control/dashboard.ts`. (1) `GET /v1/home` and `GET /v1/runs/<run>/overview` give the screens' words as data. The words are still made by page code (`src/control/ui/words/`, the cards of what needs the owner), so page code registers the two routes (`src/control/dashboard/app/`); they move to the API when the words leave page code (goals 244, 246 and 247). (2) `GET /v1/stream` says only that something changed: control compares, every 2 seconds, a mark of what the rigs reported and of the audit log's newest entry. Goal 244's stream, which says what changed, takes its place. (3) A change that an existing route records is still named `owner:api` in the audit log when a session made it; goal 244 gives each action its caller.
- 2026-11-10: **The app's packages are its own** (`web/package.json`, `web/package-lock.json`), not a workspace of the root's: control's and the rigs' images take none of them, and the app's build stage takes none of Thermite's. `npm run web:install` installs them.
- 2026-11-10: **shadcn's tool is not one of the app's packages.** The app needs one style file of it, which is kept beside the stock components (`web/src/components/ui/tailwind.css`), with shadcn's licence. As a package the tool brought 212 packages of its own and all six findings of `npm audit`; without it the app has 190 packages and no finding. A component is added with `npx shadcn@latest add`.
- 2026-11-10: **The built app carries its licences:** `licenses.md` (the script's packages, by Vite) and `licenses-styles.md` (the fonts, the styles and the stock components), served beside it and linked from Settings › About.
- 2026-11-10: **One number for what needs the owner:** the count on Home, on the navigation and of the list are the list's rows, a rig that stopped reporting among them. The pages at `/ui` leave that rig out of their count and keep it in their list.
- 2026-11-10: **A screen's parts follow the room the screen has** (container queries), not the window's width, since the navigation takes part of the window at a tablet's width.
- 2026-11-10: **For a real control:** the stream's answer tells a proxy not to hold its lines back (`X-Accel-Buffering: no`), and Install on one machine says what a proxy must do for it; a tab nobody looks at reads nothing, and reads once when it is looked at again; an ID is copied the older way where a page over plain HTTP has no clipboard, and is selected where nothing copies.
- 2026-11-10: **What is not built here yet opens its page at `/ui`,** marked with an arrow: Live, Rigs, a need's own page, New campaign, a campaign's page, a run's other tabs, Library, Usage, Logs, and each tab of Settings but About.

## What the browser loads

The built app, 2026-11-10, as Vite writes it (`npm run web:build`):

| File | Size | Compressed (gzip) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The script, one file | 468 kB | 147 kB |
| The styles, one file | 76 kB | 13 kB |
| Geist, Latin | 29 kB | a font file is compressed already |
| Geist Mono, Latin | 23 kB | the same |

The fonts' other alphabets (Latin Extended, Cyrillic, Vietnamese, symbols; 95 kB in nine files) load only when a screen shows a character of theirs. Control serves each file under `assets/` to be kept for a year, since its name changes with its content, so a second visit loads the page alone. Control does not compress its answers; a proxy in front of it may.

## Open questions

- None. Both of the plan's questions have their answers in Decisions: a stock component's style and the policy, and how the browser check gets the app.

